# Normalise line endings at the repository boundary.
#
## Why this file exists
#
# `biome.json` sets `"lineEnding": "lf"`, so `bun run format:check` requires LF.
# Without a `.gitattributes`, the line ending a file gets is whatever the
# cloning machine's `core.autocrlf` happens to be. This repository was
# developed on Windows, where `core.autocrlf=true` is common (it is set at
# system level on the development machine), so a fresh clone rewrote every LF
# blob to CRLF on checkout and Biome rejected all ~399 code files.
#
# That is why `format:check` failed on every CI run on `main` from 2026-09-05
# onward, while passing in the original working tree, where the files had
# never been round-tripped through a fresh checkout.
#
# Declaring the endings here makes the result depend on the repository rather
# than on whoever clones it. The blobs in git were already LF; this keeps them
# LF on the way out, for every platform.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native binaries must never be translated, or git will corrupt them.
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite-wal binary
*.sqlite-shm binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Lockfiles and generated assets are not worth normalising.
bun.lockb binary
